From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Anton Palgunov <toxblh@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 08:50:44 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 85/99] v8: e2k: select Word32, Float32 and Float64 values with
 merge

Declare kWord32Select, kFloat32Select and kFloat64Select. A Word32
select is the Word64 one (the values are sign-extended either way).
Floating-point registers are general registers on e2k, so a float select
is the same compare and merge on the predicate (fsel after a floating-
point compare); the selector gives its values in registers and makes it
only on a compare, a bit test or a floating-point compare.
Math.round (Float64Round) and Math.sign lower to such selects.
